  "answer": "This feature request has been made before. A hotkey that turns the screen off instantly, without sleeping or locking, doesn't exist in PowerToys yet. The older requests were closed as duplicates of the tracking issue PowerToys#1052 (Quick Display adjustment), which lists \"sleep monitors\". Until it's built, you have these workarounds. (1) Make a shortcut that runs `powershell (Add-Type '[DllImport(\\\"user32.dll\\\")]public static extern int PostMessage(int hWnd, int hMsg, int wParam, int lParam);' -Name a -Pas)::PostMessage(-1,0x0112,0xF170,2)` and give it a keyboard shortcut. (2) Use AutoHotkey or `nircmd.exe monitor off` bound to a hotkey. (3) Use Twinkle Tray, which can turn monitors off with a hotkey. In all of these, moving the mouse or pressing a key wakes the display, and the PC keeps running, so your render isn't interrupted. Your Windows sign-in settings may require you to sign in again after the display wakes. Also add a thumbs-up to the existing issues instead of opening a new one."
 },
